WEBVTT

00:00:02.176 --> 00:00:05.179
SINGER:
No, don't let

00:00:07.098 --> 00:00:11.310
This magic die

00:00:13.104 --> 00:00:16.065
The answer's there

00:00:17.566 --> 00:00:20.778
[BELL TOLLING]
[BIRDS CAWING]

00:00:47.596 --> 00:00:49.724
[GRUNTING]

00:01:14.165 --> 00:01:16.250
VOLDEMORT:
Let me see it again.

00:01:17.626 --> 00:01:20.504
Yes, the time is close now.

00:01:25.176 --> 00:01:27.178
Harry, at last!

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:33.768
Step aside, Wormtail,
so I can give our guest a proper greeting.

00:01:35.019 --> 00:01:36.395
[PANTING]

00:01:36.645 --> 00:01:38.773
[FLOORBOARDS CREAKING]

00:01:44.278 --> 00:01:45.780
You all right, Harry?

00:01:47.198 --> 00:01:49.033
I just got in.

00:01:49.533 --> 00:01:50.868
Me.

00:01:55.623 --> 00:01:58.209
[HUMS]

00:02:02.171 --> 00:02:05.299
HERMIONE: Harry, you told me
you'd figured the egg out weeks ago.

00:02:05.549 --> 00:02:09.678
-The task is two days from now.
-Really? I had no idea.

00:02:11.222 --> 00:02:13.140
I suppose Viktor's
already figured it out.

00:02:13.224 --> 00:02:16.185
Wouldn't know. We don't actually
talk about the tournament.

00:02:17.228 --> 00:02:21.941
Actually, we don't really talk at all.
Viktor's more of a physical being.

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:24.235
[LAUGHS]

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:28.823
I just mean he's not
particularly loquacious.

00:02:29.073 --> 00:02:31.450
-Mm-hm.
-Mostly, he watches me study.

00:02:32.243 --> 00:02:34.328
It's a bit annoying, actually.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:38.457
You are trying to figure this egg out,
aren't you?

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.835
What's that supposed to mean?

00:02:41.335 --> 00:02:44.338
It just means these tasks
are designed to test you...

00:02:44.588 --> 00:02:47.716
...in the most brutal way.
They're almost cruel.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.469
And...

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:54.723
...I'm scared for you.

00:02:55.724 --> 00:02:58.269
You got by the dragons
mostly on nerve.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:01.355
I'm not sure it's going
to be enough this time.

00:03:01.605 --> 00:03:03.274
CEDRIC:
Hey, Potter!

00:03:09.113 --> 00:03:10.489
-Potter!
HARRY: Cedric.

00:03:13.284 --> 00:03:14.952
How--? How are you?

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.288
Spectacular.

00:03:18.956 --> 00:03:20.541
I realize I never really
thanked you properly

00:03:20.583 --> 00:03:22.751
for tipping me off about those dragons.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:25.296
Forget it. I'm sure you
would've done the same for me.

00:03:25.504 --> 00:03:27.256
Exactly.

00:03:28.299 --> 00:03:30.718
You know the Prefects' bathroom
on the fifth floor?

00:03:34.638 --> 00:03:37.308
It's not a bad place for a bath.

00:03:39.518 --> 00:03:41.395
Just take your egg...

00:03:42.313 --> 00:03:45.024
...and mull things over
in the hot water.

00:04:20.309 --> 00:04:22.353
I must be out of my mind.

00:04:25.189 --> 00:04:27.524
[SCREECHING]

00:04:32.446 --> 00:04:34.698
I'm definitely out of my mind.

00:04:35.157 --> 00:04:37.076
[GIRL GIGGLING]

00:04:37.368 --> 00:04:40.579
I'd try putting it in the water
if I were you.

00:04:40.829 --> 00:04:42.665
Myrtle!

00:04:42.831 --> 00:04:44.583
Hello, Harry.

00:04:45.376 --> 00:04:48.587
Long time no see.

00:04:48.796 --> 00:04:50.714
Oh.

00:04:50.965 --> 00:04:52.591
[GIGGLING]

00:04:52.841 --> 00:04:56.470
I was circling a blocked drain
the other day...

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:00.224
...and could swear I saw a bit
of Polyjuice Potion.

00:05:00.391 --> 00:05:02.601
Not being a bad boy again,
are you, Harry?

00:05:02.851 --> 00:05:04.561
Polyjuice Potion?

00:05:05.396 --> 00:05:09.400
Kicked the habit. Myrtle, did you say,
"Try putting it in the water"?

00:05:09.566 --> 00:05:12.403
[SQUEALS]

00:05:13.195 --> 00:05:14.863
[COUGHING]

00:05:16.365 --> 00:05:17.866
That's what he did.

00:05:18.742 --> 00:05:20.411
The other boy...

00:05:21.829 --> 00:05:23.872
...the handsome one...

00:05:25.249 --> 00:05:26.458
...Cedric.

00:05:29.837 --> 00:05:32.423
Well, go on. Open it.

00:05:40.514 --> 00:05:45.519
WOMAN [SINGING]: Come seek us
Where our voices sound

00:05:45.769 --> 00:05:50.441
We cannot sing
Above the ground

00:05:50.524 --> 00:05:54.903
An hour long you'll have to look

00:05:55.654 --> 00:06:00.451
To recover what we took

00:06:01.452 --> 00:06:03.287
[COUGHING]

00:06:06.457 --> 00:06:08.417
[MIMICS COUGHING]

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:10.127
Myrtle...

00:06:11.462 --> 00:06:14.465
...there aren't merpeople
in the Black Lake, are there?

00:06:14.548 --> 00:06:17.468
Oh, very good.

00:06:18.427 --> 00:06:22.681
It took Cedric ages to riddle it out.

00:06:23.307 --> 00:06:26.935
Almost all the bubbles were gone.

00:06:29.438 --> 00:06:31.273
[GROWLS]

00:06:31.482 --> 00:06:33.942
[GIGGLES]

00:06:34.485 --> 00:06:37.321
[SQUEALING]

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:41.075
Oh, Harry.

00:06:44.578 --> 00:06:46.580
Harry, tell me again.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:48.207
[RON SNORING]

00:06:48.457 --> 00:06:51.210
"Come seek us
where our voices sound."

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:54.546
The Black Lake, that's obvious.

00:06:54.963 --> 00:06:57.424
"An hour long you'll have to look."

00:06:57.508 --> 00:07:01.053
Again, obvious. Though, admittedly,
potentially problematic.

00:07:02.513 --> 00:07:04.348
"Potentially problematic"?

00:07:04.515 --> 00:07:07.601
When's the last time you held your breath
underwater for an hour, Hermione?

00:07:08.352 --> 00:07:12.523
Look, Harry, we can do this.
The three of us can figure it out.

00:07:12.731 --> 00:07:15.359
MOODY:
Hate to break up the skull session.

00:07:15.526 --> 00:07:17.528
Professor McGonagall
wants you in her office.

00:07:17.611 --> 00:07:20.072
Not you, Potter,
just Weasley and Granger.

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:22.866
But, sir, the second task
is only hours away, and--

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:25.619
Exactly. Presumably Potter
is well prepared by now...

00:07:25.828 --> 00:07:27.621
...and could do with
a good night's sleep.

00:07:27.871 --> 00:07:30.499
Go. Now!

00:07:40.467 --> 00:07:42.219
Longbottom!
